language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ csplib_005_autocorrelation: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Construct a binary sequence of length n, each bit +1 or -1, that minimizes the autocorrelations between bits, with periodic (cyclic) boundary conditions. The k-th autocorrelation is C_k = sum over i from 0 to n-1 of S_i * S_((i+k) mod n), for k from 1 to n-1. The aim is to minimize E = sum over k from 1 to n-1 of C_k^2.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `csplib_005_autocorrelation.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/csplib_005_autocorrelation.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `csplib_005_autocorrelation_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py csplib_005_autocorrelation.json
$   savilerow model.eprime csplib_005_autocorrelation_1.param -run-solver

$ n: the length of the sequence
given n : int(2..)

$ sequence[i]: bit i of the sequence (indices 1-based, so the reference's S_0 is sequence[1]), +1 or -1
find sequence : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(-1..1)
$ C[k]: the k-th periodic autocorrelation of the sequence (k from 1 to n-1)
find C : matrix indexed by [int(1..n-1)] of int(-n..n)

minimising sum k : int(1..n-1) . C[k] * C[k]
such that
$ every bit is +1 or -1, so no bit is 0
forAll i : int(1..n) . sequence[i] != 0,
$ the k-th autocorrelation is the sum of the products of bits that are k apart, wrapping around at the end (j = i+k, or j = i+k-n after wrapping)
forAll k : int(1..n-1) . C[k] = (sum i : int(1..n) . sum j : int(1..n) . toInt(j = i + k \/ j = i + k - n) * sequence[i] * sequence[j])
